    "details": "The Erlang/OTP project reports:\n\n> OTP 29.1.2, 28.5.0.8 and 27.3.4.19 fix the following issues, three of\n> which complete earlier incomplete fixes:\n>\n> - CVE-2026-105236: (D)TLS-1.2 session resumption could cross SNI\n>   virtual-host boundaries. An SNI-aware server resumed a cached\n>   session even when the resumption request\\'s server_name differed\n>   from the one that established it, so a client could bypass the\n>   client-authentication boundary of a second virtual service and skip\n>   the certificate exchange.\n> - CVE-2026-94200: a malicious or man-in-the-middle TLS-1.3 server\n>   could poison a client\\'s ticket store with a NewSessionTicket\n>   carrying a zero-length early_data extension. A client using\n>   automatic session-ticket management stored the ticket and crashed on\n>   a later resumption, taking down the node-global client ticket store.\n> - CVE-2026-42789: the earlier fix for certificate chain forgery via\n>   non-CA intermediates in public_key left the X.509 version 1 and\n>   version 2 path uncovered. Such certificates carry no\n>   basicConstraints and are now rejected in issuer position.\n> - CVE-2026-48856: the earlier fix for credential leaks on cross-origin\n>   httpc redirects did not clear the userinfo component of the request\n>   URI, so credentials given as http://user:password@host/path were\n>   still sent to the redirect target.\n> - CVE-2026-70405: the earlier byte-length bounds on snmp varbind\n>   values did not cover the v3 header fields, the USM security\n>   parameters or the PDU integer fields, which could still be decoded\n>   into arbitrarily large integers.\n",
